From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:08:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: Plugins has a Kiln OS tab and a Community tab

Kiln's plugin catalog now lists plugins made by other people next to
Kiln's own, and printer.ad5x_plugins marks them: catalog[<name>] and
available[<name>] carry "community" (true when the plugin is not from
one of Kiln's own repositories, also for one installed by hand) and
"author" (catalog: also the pinned "commit"). Settings > Plugins
(patch 0005) showed them in one list with Kiln's, with nothing to tell
them apart.

Two tabs under the header, half the width each and as tall as it
(400x56 at 800x480): Kiln OS, Kiln's own plugins as before, and
Community, the plugins with community set. Each keeps the INSTALLED
and AVAILABLE groups and the STATUS group above them. Community starts
with a heading and the line "Made and supported by their authors. You
can turn them off at any time."; its rows are at least 80 px tall and
show "By {author}" under the title (plugin.json's author, else the
catalog's; no line without one) and, for a plugin with root scripts, a
key and the word Root (a key drawn from three boxes: the icon font has
none). Kiln's rows are unchanged. An empty Community group says "No
community plugins installed" or "No community plugins in the catalog".
Each open starts on Kiln OS. Without the new fields (an older Kiln OS)
every plugin is Kiln's and the Community tab is empty.

The first tap on Community shows "About community plugins" ("These
plugins are made by members of the Kiln OS community. Each author looks
after their own plugin, and every update passes Kiln's automated checks
before it's offered. Questions or problems? The author's page is the
best place to ask. You can turn off or remove a plugin any time.") with
Got it and Back. Got it opens
the tab and keeps that in HelixScreen's settings
(/ad5x_plugins/community_notice_seen), so it shows once; Back, or a tap
beside the dialog, stays on Kiln OS and remembers nothing.

Patch 0097's root confirmation gets one more paragraph for a community
plugin: "This plugin needs root access, so it can change system files.
Install it only if you trust the author." Kiln's own root plugins ask
as before.

The tab filter, the AVAILABLE state per tab, the author line, the
notice's steps and the confirmation come from small helpers
(ad5x_installed_plugins/ad5x_catalog_plugins with a tab,
ad5x_catalog_state, ad5x_author_line, ad5x_tab_step,
ad5x_community_notice_answer, ad5x_toggle_confirm), so the tests can
check them.

The new strings are in every language. The rest of the Plugins screen
(the group headers, the status lines, the Built-in tag, the install,
update and remove questions) was only in English and Russian; it is
added in the other nine, so the tabs do not sit beside English text.
Catalog titles and descriptions and Klipper's own messages stay as
Klipper sends them.

The overlay now has buttons of its own (the tabs), so the toolhead
census (test_job_holds_machine.cpp) lists it among the files whose
controls move nothing; the rows' switches and buttons are counted in
their own files as before.

Tests: each tab lists only its plugins, in the installed and the
catalog groups, and a tab's AVAILABLE state counts only its catalog
entries; an object without the fields puts everything on Kiln OS;
"By {author}" is shown with an author (plugin.json's, else the
catalog's) and left out without one; the notice is asked until Got it,
Back keeps Kiln OS and asks again, and after Got it the tab opens
straight away; the trust line is in the root confirmation of
a community plugin only, not for Kiln's root plugins, not for a
community plugin without root scripts and not when turning off; in
every language the notice, its buttons, the author line, the trust
line and the Plugins screen's sentences are translated (Russian
checked word for word).
